    "turn_text": "Well, I think, first of all, I'm not being too subjective about this. I think is my writing this book and going out as a former president to talk about it, because a lot of people are startled, actually. You know, when I give them the facts that are proven by origins in the book, sources of the information, including the U.S. State Department, I also wrote the Popolata and told Pope Francis that that I had met previously with his predecessor with Pope John Paul II about these issues. I found him to be very conservative on the issue, but I got a letter from Pope Francis that said that he thought there were a lot of things in my book with which he would help, like slavery and prostitution and things of that kind. I didn't ask him to permit women to be priests in the Catholic Church. That's too big a step to take it once. But he did respond to my letter by saying it is his opinion In the future, women needed to play a much greater role in the Catholic Church itself, which was very encouraging to me. And last week, as you may have noticed, he appointed an eight-person committee to deal with the abuse of children by priests and four of those eight more women, which was quite startling. And one of them was a woman who had been abused by a priest when she was a child in a convent. So the religious leaders and the political leaders, and one thing I advocate in the book, I've got 23 recommendations at the end of the book to deal with all the issues that I've thought to you about and had so much that still in the book. One of those is to take away from commanding officers in the military. Any right to have struck the prosecution, a prosecution of a alleged rapist. Now the commanding officers can block that, as you know. And the senator from New York tried to change that, unsuccessful. Although she did get 55 votes in the Senate, she didn't get the 60 required. But you know, if our top political leaders that the President and others would just join in with her, which they didn't do, I think we could maybe do that and we could do away with, so we could certainly reduce the level of human trafficking or trading in slavery that exists on a global basis.",
